    "id": "veggie-smash-burger",
    "title": "Veggie smash burger",
    "category": "Pasta & Noodles",
    "protein": "Chicken",
    "servings": 4,
    "prepTime": "10 mins",
    "cookTime": "120 mins",
    "totalTime": "130 mins",
    "calories": 608,
    "macros": {
      "protein_g": 38,
      "carbs_g": 69,
      "fat_g": 20
    },
    "micros": {
      "fiber_g": 8,
      "sodium_mg": 520,
      "iron_mg": 2.0,
      "potassium_mg": 670,
      "vitamin_c_mg": 27,
      "calcium_mg": 200
    },
    "ingredients": [
      "This recipe is Gordon Ramsay's Slow-Roasted Pork Belly with Fennel, featured in his Ultimate Cookery Course.",
      "1 kg (2.2 lbs) pork belly, skin-on",
      "1 bulb fresh fennel, trimmed and roughly sliced",
      "1 tbsp fennel seeds",
      "4 fresh bay leaves",
      "3 garlic cloves, peeled and bashed",
      "1 tsp cardamom pods, bashed",
      "4 whole star anise",
      "325 ml (1⅓ cups) dry white wine",
      "500–750 ml (2–3 cups) chicken stock",
      "1 tbsp wholegrain mustard",
      "Olive oil, sea salt, and black pepper",
      "Pasta: 1 lb cavatappi (or corkscrew pasta)",
      "Cheese Blend (2.5 lbs total — freshly hand-grate and mix together):",
      "16 oz (1 lb) Mozzarella",
      "16 oz (1 lb) Colby Jack",
      "8 oz Sharp Cheddar",
      "Seasoning Mix (combine in a small bowl):",
      "1 tsp garlic powder",
      "1 tsp smoked paprika",
      "½ tsp salt",
      "½ tsp freshly ground black or white pepper",
      "Sauce Base:",
      "3 tbsp unsalted butter",
      "3 tbsp all-purpose flour",
      "12 oz (1 can) evaporated milk",
      "2 cups heavy cream",
      "1 tbsp Dijon mustard"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Score and season the pork",
      "Preheat your oven to 180°C (350°F). Score the skin in a diamond pattern at 1.5 cm intervals with a sharp knife. Bending the meat slightly to open the cuts, rub in a generous amount of sea salt and black pepper so it penetrates deep into the meat.",
      "Sear aromatics and pork",
      "Requires a stovetop-safe roasting tray",
      "Place a roasting tray on the stovetop over medium heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Add sliced fennel, bay leaves, garlic, cardamom, star anise, and half of the fennel seeds. Fry for 2 minutes until fragrant. Push aromatics to the edges, place the pork skin-side down, and sear for 5 minutes until golden brown.",
      "Add braising liquids",
      "Keep liquid below the top skin line",
      "Flip the pork skin-side up, season the skin with another pinch of salt, and sprinkle over the remaining fennel seeds. Pour in the white wine to deglaze the tray without getting the skin wet. Bring to a boil, then pour in enough chicken stock to reach just below the top layer of fat.",
      "Slow-roast in the oven",
      "Roast uncovered for 2 hours 30 minutes",
      "Transfer the uncovered tray to the preheated oven. Cook for 2.5 hours until the skin turns golden and crisp, and the meat becomes tender.",
      "Rest the meat and make pan gravy",
      "Transfer the pork to a cutting board to rest. Skim off excess fat from the pan juices (or drag a slice of bread across the surface to absorb it). Place the tray back on the hob over medium heat, whisk in the wholegrain mustard, and simmer until reduced into a rich sauce. Strain and serve alongside carved slices.",
      "YouTube video views will be stored in your YouTube History, and your data will be stored and used by YouTube according to its Terms of Service",
      "This is the exact recipe for Chef Tini’s viral Mac & Cheese (@Tiniyounger), famous for its ultra-creamy, roux-based sauce, heavy cheese pull, and golden baked crust.",
      "Prep Pasta, Cheese, & Spices",
      "Hand-grating block cheese is critical to prevent graininess",
      "Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C) and grease a 9x13-inch baking dish.",
      "Boil the cavatappi in salted water until al dente (about 1–2 minutes under package directions). Drain and set aside.",
      "Hand-grate all three cheeses, mix them together in a large bowl, and divide into two equal portions (half for the sauce, half for layering).",
      "Combine the garlic powder, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper in a small bowl, then divide into two equal portions.",
      "Build the Seasoned Roux",
      "Melt 3 tbsp butter in a large pot or deep skillet over medium heat.",
      "Stir in half of the seasoning mix to bloom the spices in the hot butter for ~30 seconds.",
      "Sprinkle in 3 tbsp all-purpose flour. Whisk continuously for 1 to 2 minutes until bubbling and pale golden to cook out the raw flour taste.",
      "Create the Cream Base",
      "Slowly stream in the 12 oz can of evaporated milk while whisking constantly to prevent lumps.",
      "Pour in the 2 cups of heavy cream, the remaining half of the seasoning mix, and 1 tbsp Dijon mustard.",
      "Continue whisking over medium heat until the mixture comes to a gentle simmer and thickens slightly (approx. 2–3 minutes).",
      "Melt the Cheese Sauce",
      "Keep heat low to prevent sauce separation",
      "Turn heat to low. Add half of the total shredded cheese gradually, adding one small handful at a time.",
      "Whisk thoroughly after each handful until completely melted and smooth before adding the next.",
      "Once the sauce is velvety, remove from heat and fold in the cooked cavatappi until fully coated.",
      "Layer, Bake, & Broil",
      "Spread half of the cheesy pasta into the bottom of the prepared baking dish.",
      "Sprinkle half of the remaining reserved cheese evenly over the layer.",
      "Add the remaining pasta, then top with the rest of the shredded cheese.",
      "Bake at 350°F for 25–30 minutes until bubbly around the edges.",
      "Switch oven to broil for 2 minutes to get a golden-brown top crust. Let rest 5–10 minutes before serving."
    ],
